# Generated by StepForge — by Md Zarin Tasnim · Prepared by Md Zarin Tasnim · 2026-10-07
Feature: Shop › Checkout
  Shop Desk, Staging environment.

  @smoke @checkout-flow @p1
  Scenario Outline: Checkout with every UI step
    Covers the whole UI catalogue.
    Given A product is in stock
    # Sign in as admin
    When open /login
    And type "<user>" into the "Email" field
    And type "{{secret.adminPassword}}" into the field with placeholder "Password"
    And click the "Sign in" button
    # Open the cart
    And open /cart
    And open {{env.baseUrl}}/products?region={{env.region}}
    Then title contains "Products"
    When click the element "product-1"
    Then url matches "/products/\d+"
    When double-click "Zoom image"
    And right-click the element ".gallery img"
    And hover over the "Details" link
    And type "blue <qty>" into the "Search" field
    And clear the "Search" field
    And type "<qty>" into the element "qty"
    Then value is "<qty>"
    When press Enter in the element "qty"
    And press Control+A
    And select "express" in the "Shipping" field
    And select "Gift wrap" in the "Extras" field
    And select "2" in the "Country" field
    And tick the "I agree" checkbox
    And untick the "Newsletter" checkbox
    And upload fixtures/invoice.pdf to the "Attachment" field
    And drag the element "item-a" onto the element "basket"
    And scroll down the page
    And scroll to the element "footer"
    And accept the next browser dialog
    And click the element "//button[@id='remove']"
    And dismiss the next browser dialog
    And switch into the frame "iframe#payment"
    And type "4242 4242 4242 4242" into the field with placeholder "Card number"
    And return to the main page
    And click the "Terms" link
    And switch to the new tab
    And wait for the page to load
    And close the current tab
    And switch to the new tab
    And wait until the element "spinner" is hidden
    And wait for the URL **/checkout/*
    And take a screenshot of the page
    And take a screenshot of the element "total"
    And read the text of the element "total" (save as total)
    And read the attribute of the "Invoice" link (save as invoiceUrl)
    And read the count of the element ".line-item" (save as lines)
    And read the url of the page (save as here)
    Then the "Order confirmed" heading is visible
    And the element "error" is hidden
    And the element "greeting" reads "Thank you, <user>!"
    And the element "total" contains "{{vars.total}}"
    And the element "order-id" matches /^ORD-\d{6}$/
    And the "Shipping" field has the value "express"
    And there are 2 × the element ".line-item"
    And check an attribute of the element "cart" equals "false"
    And the "Pay" button is enabled
    And the "Undo" button is disabled
    And the "I agree" checkbox is checked
    And the "Newsletter" checkbox is not checked
    And the URL is "/orders/done"
    And the URL contains "done"
    And the page title is "Order confirmed"
    And the page title contains "confirmed"
    When click the element "receipt"
    Then text does not contain "Error"
    When ui visualCheckpoint

    Examples:
      | id         | user          | qty |
      | TC-CHE-001 | ana@shop.test | 2   |
      | TC-CHE-002 | ben@shop.test | 1   |
